{
  "schema_version": 3,
  "id": "2026-09-25-model-catalog-sync-read-per-mount",
  "problem_type": "Selecting a canvas card re-reads, re-migrates and re-decrypts the whole model catalog over sync IPC many times per mount",
  "symptom": "Creating a video node or starting a drag on an unselected card stalls the frame (new node longest frame 71–102 ms, drag start 69–73 ms on 32 × 1080p). The prompt composer mounts on select and blocks the renderer on sync IPC.",
  "direct_cause": "useChannelCreateBodies computed channel bodies twice per mount (useState initializer + an immediate effect recompute) and called listMappings once per mode and once per guidance candidate (7–12 sync IPC per mount). On the main side every call went through readCatalog, which re-read, re-parsed, migrated and decrypted every vendor key of a 300 KB file, then deep-cloned it before filtering.",
  "class_root": "The catalog read choke point (readCatalog) had no notion of \"unchanged since last read\", and the renderer had no per-computation reuse, so the cost of a read scaled with the number of callers instead of with catalog changes.",
  "affected_population": [
    "Every desktop user selecting or creating a generation node (composer mount), worse with many vendors or a large catalog",
    "Every main-process reader of readCatalog (52 call sites) pays a full re-parse and decrypt per call"
  ],
  "scope_paths": [
    "electron/catalog/catalogStore.ts",
    "electron/catalog/catalogFileAccess.ts",
    "src/workbench/generationCanvas/nodes/controls/useChannelCreateBody.ts",
    "src/workbench/generationCanvas/nodes/controls/narrowedModeGuidance.ts"
  ],
  "entry_points": [
    "Composer mount on node select / new node (NodeParameterControls → useChannelCreateBodies)",
    "Narrowed-mode guidance across candidate channels (useNarrowedModeGuidance)",
    "Every main-process readCatalog caller (IPC list/health/upsert paths, generation providers)"
  ],
  "external_sources": [
    {
      "kind": "official-doc",
      "url": "https://www.electronjs.org/docs/latest/tutorial/ipc",
      "checked_at": "2026-09-25",
      "purpose": "Electron documents sendSync as blocking the renderer until the main process replies; each sync read is a frame-blocking round trip, so the count per mount matters."
    }
  ],
  "invariants": [
    "readCatalog re-parses and decrypts only when the file bytes changed, or when a key could not be decrypted (locked keychain is never cached)",
    "Write flows always receive a private deep copy; read-only lists share a deep-frozen snapshot, and mutating it throws",
    "One composer computation asks each vendor for its mappings at most once"
  ],
  "invariant_owner_layer": {
    "layer": "electron/catalog/catalogStore.ts",
    "tests": [
      "electron/catalog/catalogReadCache.test.ts"
    ],
    "why": "readCatalog is the single read choke point of the catalog file; the cache and the frozen shared snapshot live there, so every reader inherits them."
  },
